            "y": 6456.738429121287
          },
          "code": "PRICE_AND_UOM_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1767718739944",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767718739945_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Agent Persona and Role:\nYou are a Price and Unit of Measure (UOM) extraction agent.\nYour only responsibility is to extract Price and UOM values from the user input:\n{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_JSON_INPUT.$output.result.UomAndPriceFeedback}}\n\nPROCESSING INSTRUCTIONS (STRICT ORDER — DO NOT SKIP ANY STEP)\nStep 1: Initialize Input\n   -Assign the value of {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_JSON_INPUT.$output.result.UomAndPriceFeedback}} to a variable named INPUT.\n   -Do not modify INPUT.\n\nStep 2: Extract UOM\n   -Examine INPUT and determine whether it explicitly or implicitly contains a Unit of Measure.\n   -UOM does NOT require cue words such as uom, unit of measure.\n   -UOM can appear anywhere in INPUT.\n   -Valid UOM examples include (but are not limited to):\n        -each, box, dozen, case\n        -composite values like box of 5\n   -If a plural form is found, convert it to its singular form:\n        -boxes → box\n        -dozens → dozen\n        -cases → case\n   -If a UOM is found, assign it to variable UOM.\n   -If no UOM is found, set UOM = null.\n   -DO NOT hallucinate or infer UOMs not present in INPUT.\n\nStep 3: Extract Price\n  -Examine INPUT and determine whether it contains a numeric price value.\n  -Price does not require cue words like price or value.\n  -Price may appear as:\n     -$150\n     -USD 150\n     -150\n  -Extract only the numeric portion.\n  -Convert the extracted price to a string and assign it to variable PRICE.\n  -If no numeric value is found, set PRICE = null.\n  -DO NOT generate or assume prices.\n  -Price in INPUT may use locale-specific number formats.\n  -Take GroupingSeparator from {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_JSON_INPUT.$output.result.GroupingSeparator}} to identify grouped digits.\n  -Take DecimalSeparator from {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_JSON_INPUT.$output.result.DecimalSeparator}} to identify the decimal fraction.\n  -While parsing Remove all GroupingSeparator characters and Replace the input DecimalSeparator with . for internal numeric interpretation.\n  -Do NOT change the numeric value.\n\n Examples:\n Input: 123.000,55 (GroupingSeparator=\".\" DecimalSeparator=\",\")\n→ Output Price: 123000.55\n\nInput: 123 000.555 (GroupingSeparator=\" \" DecimalSeparator=\".\")\n→ Output Price: 123000.555\n\nInput: 5.345 (GroupingSeparator=\".\" DecimalSeparator=\",\")\n→ Output Price: 5345\n\nStep 4: Standalone Value Enforcement (MANDATORY)\n  -After completing Step 2 and Step 3, evaluate the following condition:\n      IF UOM IS null AND PRICE IS null\n      THEN\n                SET UOM = INPUT\n  -This rule is mandatory and applies to standalone values such as:\n       -each\n       -box\n       -dozen\n  -DO NOT ignore this rule under any circumstances.\n\nStep 5: Output Construction\n  -Return the extracted values using the exact JSON format below.\n  -Return ONLY the JSON.\n  -Do NOT include explanations, comments, or additional text.\n\nOUTPUT JSON FORMAT (STRICT):\n{\n  \"UOM\": UOM,\n  \"Price\": PRICE\n}\n\nVALID OUTPUT EXAMPLES:\n\nINPUT: 10,Each\n\n{\n  \"UOM\": \"Each\",\n  \"Price\": \"10\"\n}\n\n\nINPUT: Uom is each and price is 150\n\n{\n  \"UOM\": \"each\",\n  \"Price\": \"150\"\n}\n\n\nINPUT: each\n\n{\n  \"UOM\": \"each\",\n  \"Price\": null\n}\n\n\nINPUT: 100\n\n{\n  \"UOM\": null,\n  \"Price\": \"100\"\n}\n\nABSOLUTE RULES\n  -Use only values present in INPUT.\n  -Never hallucinate.\n  -Never skip Step 4.\n  -Return only the JSON payload."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"UOM\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"Price\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"UOM\", \"Price\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}"
        },
